    "kind": "definition_of_done",
    "summary": "- Invite tokens are 32 random bytes from `crypto/rand` in unpadded base64url. Only the SHA-256 hash is stored and persisted in snapshots. The plaintext appears only in the invitation email, and no POST, GET, or snapshot output contains it.\n- Accept returns 404 `invite_not_found` for unknown or revoked tokens, 410 `invite_used` for accepted ones, and 410 `invite_expired` after 7 days on the service clock. Re-inviting an address (case-insensitive) revokes the older pending invites. `GET /v1/invites` lists only pending invites, each with `expires_at`.\n- Checked by `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`\n...[truncated]",
